              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "MSNBC officially rebranded to **MS NOW** (an acronym for *My Source for News, Opinion, and the World*). This change occurred after the network was spun off from NBCUniversal/Comcast into a new, independent company called **Versant Media Group**. Despite the new name and logo, the network maintains the exact same lineup of hosts (including Rachel Maddow, Lawrence O\u2019Donnell, Ari Melber, and Nicolle Wallace) and progressive news focus.\n\nWhile there is no official, 100% free 24/7 live **video** stream of the channel without a television subscription, there are several legal, high-quality ways to stream MS NOW (MSNBC) online for free or at a low cost:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Free Audio Streaming (100% Free & Unlimited)\nIf you only want to listen to the live news coverage, analysis, and prime-time commentary, you can stream the **live audio broadcast for free**:\n* **TuneIn Radio:** The TuneIn app and website host a legal, official 24/7 live audio stream of MS NOW (MSNBC) that is completely free to listen to. \n\n### 2. Free Trials via Live TV Streaming Services\nYou can watch the live video feed of MS NOW for free by utilizing the free trials offered by major live TV streaming services. **Remember to cancel before the trial period ends to avoid being charged**:\n* **DirecTV Stream (Entertainment package):** Typically offers a **5-day free trial**. It features MS NOW in its base tier.\n* **Fubo (Pro package):** Often offers a **7-day free trial**.\n* **YouTube TV:** Regularly offers a **7- to 14-day free trial** for new users.\n* **Sling TV (Sling Blue):** While Sling TV does not always have a free trial, it is often the most budget-friendly live TV provider (usually starting around $40\u2013$45/month) to carry the channel in its \"Sling Blue\" package.\n\n### 3. Use an Existing TV Provider Login (Free if you have credentials)\nIf you, a family member, or a friend has a traditional cable, satellite, or live TV streaming subscription (like YouTube TV or Hulu + Live TV):\n* You can go to the **NBC.com** stream page or download the **MS NOW app** on your phone, tablet, or smart TV. \n* Select \"Link TV Provider\" and log in with those credentials to unlock the 24/7 live video stream for free. *(Note: The app occasionally offers a \"10-minute preview pass\" for free without a login, but it will cut off after the limit is reached).*\n\n### 4. Low-Cost Alternative: Peacock\nIf you do not want to pay for an expensive live TV package, **Peacock Premium** or **Premium Plus** offers live and on-demand segments of MS NOW shows, though it is not a completely free service. Some prime-time shows may air live or become available on-demand the next day.\n\n*Avoid unofficial or third-party streaming websites that promise \"free MSNBC online TV,\" as they are often filled with intrusive malware, pop-up ads, and unreliable, illegal feeds.*",
